{"name":"Demonic Kiss","hex":"#d02b48","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"demonic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to demons or evil spirits; demoniac.","Pertaining to daemons in ancient Greek thought; concerning supernatural ‘genius’."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demonic"},{"term":"kiss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch with the lips or press the lips against, usually to show love or affection or passion, or as part of a greeting.","To (cause to) touch lightly or slightly; to come into contact."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A touch with the lips, usually to express love or affection, or as a greeting.","An 'X' mark placed at the end of a letter or other type of message, signifying the bestowal of a kiss from the sender to the receiver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg/330px-Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/USMC-16853.jpg/500px-USMC-16853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam